meta {
  name: Stripe Webhook (Use CLI)
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

docs {
  WARNING: DO NOT TEST STRIPE WEBHOOKS VIA BRUNO!

  Unlike Xendit which used a static token, Stripe Webhooks require a cryptographic signature (`stripe-signature` header) generated dynamically from the exact raw payload and your STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET. 
  
  If you send a request via Bruno, it will fail with 401 Unauthorized because the signature will be missing or invalid.

  To test Stripe Webhooks locally, run this in your terminal:
  `stripe trigger checkout.session.completed`
}
